IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `itaa-income`

-- Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- income amounts the text deposit could not compute, now
-- computed from the formulas the Federal Register prints as images: net labour income for the working Australians tax offset
-- (s 61-155(2)); the small business income tax offset (ss 328-355, 328-357, 328-360); the income tax owed with that offset
-- (s 4-10(3)); and the tax-free part of a genuine redundancy or early retirement scheme payment (s 83-170(3)), with its base
-- and service amounts indexed annually (ss 960-270, 960-275(1A), 960-280(4)).
--
-- A module beside itaa-income.l4 (24 October 2026). itaa-income.l4's `What working Australians tax offset do I get` takes "net
-- labour income" as one supplied number, and the small business income tax offset and the redundancy amounts were not
-- encoded at all ("every tax offset other than the two named"). That module stays as it is; this one calls its rules
-- (`What is my basic income tax liability`, `What Low Income tax offset do I get`, `What working Australians tax offset do I
-- get`) rather than restating them.
--
-- SEAT: the taxpayer -- an individual Australian resident: a sole trader ("What small business offset do I get?"), a worker
-- ("What is my net labour income?"), an employee made redundant ("How much of my redundancy pay is tax-free?").
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 267 (register id C2026C00400), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A05138.txt. The
-- formulas are images the text deposit dropped; they are transcribed in ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A05138.formulas.md
-- (entries s 61-155(2), s 328-360(1), s 83-170(3), s 960-275(1A); recovered 2026-10-22 and 2026-10-24), and encoded from there.
--
-- INPUTS THAT ARE NOT LAW. s 960-280(4): for the redundancy amounts, the index number for a quarter is "the estimate of
-- full-time adult average weekly ordinary time earnings for the middle month of the quarter first published by the Australian
-- Statistician". None is deposited, so they are an input: a list of the November figures.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. What is assessable labour income, a business, personal services income (asked as facts, each summed into
-- "labour amounts"); s 61-155(3) (an amount counted once) is the person's to apply in stating the totals; the small business
-- offset for an individual under 18 (s 328-375: answered `not covered`) and for a share of a partnership's or trust's net small
-- business income (s 328-355(b), (c): the person states the reduced amount as part of their net small business income); what
-- net small business income is (s 328-365, s 328-370: asked as a fact); whether a payment is a genuine redundancy or early
-- retirement scheme payment (ss 83-175, 83-180: one fact) and the employment termination payment rules for the rest of it
-- (Division 82). Years of income are named by the calendar year in which they begin, as in itaa-income.l4.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 -- income amounts from the formulas`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller sum of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger sum of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `61-155(2) -- net labour income`

-- s 61-155(2), from the authorised rendering (C2004A05138.formulas.md):   Labour amounts − Labour deductions
-- "labour amounts means the sum of the following amounts included in your assessable income for the income year: (a) an amount
-- of *assessable labour income; (b) an amount you *derive from carrying on a *business as an individual ...; (c) an amount of
-- *personal services income; (d) an amount included in your assessable income under section 83A-25 ...; (e) [a labour hire
-- payment subject to withholding under Schedule 1 s 12-60 of the Taxation Administration Act 1953]."
-- "labour deductions means the sum of the following amounts you can deduct": losses or outgoings incurred in gaining (a) or (c),
-- necessarily incurred in a business as an individual, s 25-130, s 40-25 for assets used for (b) or (c), the standard deduction
-- in s 25-130(2)(d) to (g), and Subdivision 328-D for assets used for (b). (3): "include the amount only once".
@export What is my net labour income for the working Australians tax offset (s 61-155(2))?
GIVEN `labour amounts` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of your assessable labour income, sole-trader business income, personal services income, ESS discounts included under s 83A-25 and labour hire payments, each counted once, in dollars
      `labour deductions` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of your deductions against those amounts that s 61-155(2) lists (work expenses, business outgoings, s 25-130, depreciation on assets used for them), in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my net labour income` MEANS
    `labour amounts` MINUS `labour deductions`

-- itaa-income.l4's `What working Australians tax offset do I get` (ss 61-155(1), 61-160) on net labour income worked out above.
@export What working Australians tax offset do I get, from my labour amounts and deductions (ss 61-155, 61-160)?
GIVEN `the offset applies to the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Subdivision 61-E applies to this income year (set by the amending Act No. 49, 2026)
      `resident at any time in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were an Australian resident at any time in the income year
      `year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the income year begins
      `labour amounts` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of your labour amounts under s 61-155(2), in dollars
      `labour deductions` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of your labour deductions under s 61-155(2), in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What working Australians tax offset do I get from my labour income` MEANS
    `What working Australians tax offset do I get` `the offset applies to the year` `resident at any time in the year` `year`
        (`What is my net labour income` `labour amounts` `labour deductions`)

§§ `328-355 to 328-360 -- small business income tax offset`

-- s 328-355: "You are entitled to a *tax offset for an income year if you are an individual: (a) who is a *small business entity
-- for the income year; or (b) whose assessable income ... includes an amount that is a share of the *net small business income
-- ... of a small business entity that is not a *corporate tax entity; or (c) [a partner's or beneficiary's amount]."
-- s 328-357: for this Subdivision, a small business entity is worked out as if "each reference in section 328-110 to $10
-- million were a reference to $5 million" (aggregated turnover under $5 million; asked as one fact).
-- s 328-360(1), from the authorised rendering: "The amount of your *tax offset is equal to 16% of the following:"
--     (Your total net small business income for the income year / Your taxable income for the income year)
--         × Your basic income tax liability for the income year
-- "your total net small business income for the income year means so much of the sum of the following as does not exceed your
-- taxable income for the income year: (a) your *net small business income ...; (b) an amount referred to in paragraph 328-355(b)
-- or (c) ..., reduced (but not below zero) by your deductions to the extent that they are attributable to that amount".
-- (2): "However, the amount of your *tax offset is $1,000 if the amount worked out under subsection (1) exceeds $1,000."
-- s 328-375 (under 18): the Note to (1) says the total "will probably be worked out under section 328-375" -- not encoded.
DECLARE `Small business offset` IS ONE OF
    `offset` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered: no deposited rates for the year`
    `not covered: under 18 (s 328-375)`

@export What small business income tax offset do I get (ss 328-355, 328-357, 328-360)?
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the income year begins
      `a small business entity with turnover under $5 million, or with a share of one's net small business income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether s 328-355 entitles you (a sole trader with aggregated turnover under $5 million, or a partner or beneficiary of such a business that is not a company)
      `under 18 at the end of the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were under 18 at the end of the income year
      `net small business income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your net small business income (s 328-365) and any share under s 328-355(b) or (c) after its deductions, in dollars
      `taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your taxable income for the income year, in dollars
GIVETH A `Small business offset`
`What small business income tax offset do I get` MEANS
    IF NOT `a small business entity with turnover under $5 million, or with a share of one's net small business income` THEN `offset` 0
    ELSE IF `under 18 at the end of the year` THEN `not covered: under 18 (s 328-375)`
         ELSE IF `taxable income` AT MOST 0 THEN `offset` 0
              ELSE CONSIDER `What is my basic income tax liability` `year` `taxable income`
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered: no deposited rates for the year`
                   WHEN JUST `basic` THEN `offset` (`the smaller sum of` 1000 (`the small business share` `net small business income` `taxable income` `basic`))

GIVEN `net small business income` IS A NUMBER, `taxable income` IS A NUMBER, `basic` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the small business share` MEANS
    ((`the total net small business income` DIVIDED BY `taxable income`) TIMES `basic` TIMES 16) DIVIDED BY 100
    WHERE
        `the total net small business income` MEANS `the smaller sum of` (`the larger sum of` `net small business income` 0) `taxable income`

§§ `4-10 -- income tax owed with the small business offset`

-- s 4-10(3) Step 4 with the three offsets this encoding computes: the Low Income tax offset, the working Australians tax
-- offset and the small business income tax offset. All three fall in s 63-10 table item 20 or 3 -- not refundable, not
-- transferable, not carried forward -- so the tax owed does not go below nil. A full-year resident is assumed, as in
-- itaa-income.l4's `How much income tax do I owe`.
DECLARE `Tax owed` IS ONE OF
    `owed` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered: no deposited rates for the year, or the small business offset of someone under 18`

@export How much income tax do I owe as a full-year resident sole trader, after the Low Income, working Australians and small business offsets (ss 4-10, 328-360)?
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the income year begins
      `taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your taxable income for the income year, in dollars
      `the working Australians offset applies to the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Subdivision 61-E applies to this income year
      `labour amounts` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of your labour amounts under s 61-155(2), in dollars
      `labour deductions` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of your labour deductions under s 61-155(2), in dollars
      `a small business entity with turnover under $5 million, or with a share of one's net small business income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether s 328-355 entitles you to the small business income tax offset
      `under 18 at the end of the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were under 18 at the end of the income year
      `net small business income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your net small business income for the year, in dollars
GIVETH A `Tax owed`
`How much income tax do I owe with the small business offset` MEANS
    CONSIDER `What is my basic income tax liability` `year` `taxable income`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered: no deposited rates for the year, or the small business offset of someone under 18`
    WHEN JUST `basic` THEN
        CONSIDER `What working Australians tax offset do I get from my labour income` `the working Australians offset applies to the year` TRUE `year` `labour amounts` `labour deductions`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered: no deposited rates for the year, or the small business offset of someone under 18`
        WHEN JUST `wato` THEN
            CONSIDER `What small business income tax offset do I get` `year` `a small business entity with turnover under $5 million, or with a share of one's net small business income` `under 18 at the end of the year` `net small business income` `taxable income`
            WHEN `offset` `sbito` THEN `owed` (`the larger sum of` (`basic` MINUS (`What Low Income tax offset do I get` TRUE `taxable income`) MINUS `wato` MINUS `sbito`) 0)
            OTHERWISE `not covered: no deposited rates for the year, or the small business offset of someone under 18`

§§ `83-170 -- genuine redundancy and early retirement scheme payments`

-- s 83-170(2): "So much of the relevant payment as does not exceed the amount worked out under subsection (3) is not assessable
-- income and is not *exempt income." (3), from the authorised rendering:   Base amount + (Service amount × Years of service)
-- "base amount means: (a) for the income year 2006-2007 -- $6,783; and (b) for a later income year -- the amount mentioned in
-- paragraph (a) indexed annually." "service amount means: (a) for the income year 2006-2007 -- $3,392; and (b) ... indexed
-- annually." "years of service means the number of whole years in the period, or sum of periods, of employment to which the
-- payment relates."
-- s 960-270(1): "You index an amount by multiplying it by its *indexation factor." (2): not "if its *indexation factor is 1 or
-- less". s 960-275(1A), for items 5 and 6 of s 960-265 (the base and service amounts), from the authorised rendering:
--     Index number for the quarter ending on 31 December just before the start of the relevant income year
--         / Index number for the quarter ending on the previous 31 December
-- (5): to 3 decimal places, rounding up from a fourth decimal of 5. s 960-280(4): the index number is AWOTE "for the middle month
-- of the quarter" -- November. "Indexed annually": each year's amount is the previous year's multiplied by that year's factor, so
-- the 2007-08 amount uses November 2006 over November 2005, the 2008-09 amount November 2007 over November 2006, and so on.
-- The Act gives no rounding of the indexed amount itself; none is applied (NOTES.md, finding 12).
GIVEN `this November` IS A NUMBER, `last November` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the redundancy indexation factor` MEANS
    FLOOR ((`this November` DIVIDED BY `last November`) TIMES 1000 PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 1000

GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER, `this November` IS A NUMBER, `last November` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`indexed for one year` MEANS
    IF `the redundancy indexation factor` `this November` `last November` AT MOST 1 THEN `amount`
    ELSE `amount` TIMES `the redundancy indexation factor` `this November` `last November`

-- Index an amount through a run of November AWOTE figures, oldest first: each consecutive pair is one year's factor.
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER, `figures` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`indexed annually through` MEANS
    CONSIDER `figures`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `amount`
    WHEN `earlier` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN
        CONSIDER `rest`
        WHEN EMPTY THEN `amount`
        WHEN `later` FOLLOWED BY `others` THEN `indexed annually through` (`indexed for one year` `amount` `later` `earlier`) `rest`

DECLARE `Redundancy amount` IS ONE OF
    `tax-free` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered: the AWOTE figures do not run from November 2005 to the November before the year`
    `not covered: an income year before 2006-07`

-- The figures must run from November 2005 to November of the year before the income year: for the 2006-07 year, November 2005
-- alone (no indexing); for 2007-08, November 2005 and November 2006; and so on, one more figure each year.
@export What are the base amount and service amount for my income year, as one total for my years of service (s 83-170(3))?
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the income year of the payment begins (2026 for 2026-27)
      `November AWOTE figures from 2005` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc Full-time adult average weekly ordinary time earnings for November of each year from 2005 to the year before the income year, oldest first, as first published
      `years of service` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of whole years in the period (or periods) of employment the payment relates to
GIVETH A `Redundancy amount`
`What is my tax-free redundancy limit` MEANS
    IF `year` LESS THAN 2006 THEN `not covered: an income year before 2006-07`
    ELSE IF NOT (count `November AWOTE figures from 2005` EQUALS `year` MINUS 2005)
         THEN `not covered: the AWOTE figures do not run from November 2005 to the November before the year`
         ELSE `tax-free` (`the base amount` PLUS (`the service amount` TIMES `years of service`))
    WHERE
        `the base amount` MEANS `indexed annually through` 6783 `November AWOTE figures from 2005`
        `the service amount` MEANS `indexed annually through` 3392 `November AWOTE figures from 2005`

@export How much of my genuine redundancy or early retirement scheme payment is tax-free (s 83-170)?
GIVEN `a genuine redundancy or early retirement scheme payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment meets s 83-175 (genuine redundancy) or s 83-180 (early retirement scheme)
      `payment` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the payment, in dollars
      `year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the income year of the payment begins
      `November AWOTE figures from 2005` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc AWOTE for November of each year from 2005 to the year before, oldest first
      `years of service` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of whole years of employment the payment relates to
GIVETH A `Redundancy amount`
`How much of my redundancy payment is tax-free` MEANS
    IF NOT `a genuine redundancy or early retirement scheme payment` THEN `tax-free` 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `What is my tax-free redundancy limit` `year` `November AWOTE figures from 2005` `years of service`
         WHEN `tax-free` `limit` THEN `tax-free` (`the smaller sum of` `payment` `limit`)
         OTHERWISE `What is my tax-free redundancy limit` `year` `November AWOTE figures from 2005` `years of service`
